{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"universal windows platform universal windows platform","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md","fileName":"Universal Windows Platform.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Universal Windows Platform","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Windows Desktop Applications]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Windows Desktop Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"universal windows platform universal windows platform","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md","fileName":"Universal Windows Platform.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Universal Windows Platform","heading":"Universal Windows Platform","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The Universal Windows Platform is an application model for Windows devices that uses a defined API surface, package identity, and capability declarations. Its applications can adapt interfaces across different screen sizes and device families while sharing a common Windows codebase.\n\nCapabilities make access to sensitive device functions explicit, and packaging governs installation and distribution. UWP's constraints distinguish it from classic desktop frameworks even when both use C# and XAML.\n\nThe stock-checker and bot projects use UWP clients for Windows tablets and desktop chat. The examples combine XAML, view models, commands, and HTTP or Direct Line wrappers while keeping network and identity behavior outside the visual controls.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Windows Desktop Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"universal windows platform universal windows platform","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Universal Windows Platform.md","fileName":"Universal Windows Platform.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Universal Windows Platform","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Windows Desktop Applications","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}